==Special Moves==
====Blitz Ball====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=krauser_214a,krauser_214c,Krauser_214ac
|input=214A/C/AC
Hold 214[A]/[C]/[AC]
|input2=qcb+A/C/AC
Hold qcb+[A]/[C]/[AC]
|description3=Krauser underhands a fireball forward.
* Light version is the high fireball; faster to startup and recover, but whiffs on crouch.
* Heavy version is the low fireball; can hit crouching characters but is slow to recover, being minus on hit point blank. It also hits OTG. 
* The meterless versions have near-identical startup animations, making telling them apart extremely difficult until they come out. 
* REV version is the slowest to startup, and is the height of your average fireball. It travels slowly at first but accelerates over time. It also launches on Counter Hit. 
* Every version can be held; if held long enough, they do extra damage, are more plus on hit/block, and out-prioritize other basic projectiles. REV/Super projectiles will still beat them.
A highly variable fireball that forms the crux of Krauser's long-range game, Blitz Ball is a very daunting projectile for the opponent to navigate around in neutral. The projectiles are fast, can go high or low, and can be held to mix up the timing and make predicting them much harder. 

Each version has its own weaknesses; the light version whiffs on crouching opponents, while the heavy version is highly vulnerable to jumps. Since each version of Blitz Ball can cover the other's flaws, you will always want to alternate unpredictably between high and low, instant and held, so that it becomes harder for the opponent to predict and avoid/punish. Mixing feints into your zoning can also be quite powerful. 
}}

====Leg Tomahawk====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=krauser_236b,krauser_236d,krauser_236bd
|input=236B/D/BD
|input2=qcf+B/D/BD
|description3=Krauser does a flying axe kick that has massive range. 
* All versions are breakable before the hit, stopping Krauser short. 
* Light version becomes active faster but covers less range and is slightly minus. 
* Heavy version is slow and reactable but covers a wider range while being up to +3 on crouching block. It can also go over most standard projectiles and punish them. 
* REV version is a happy medium, being only one frame slower than the light version but has the heavy version's plus frames.
* Heavy and REV versions leave Krauser outside of close heavies' range, but surprisingly, Krauser is still left in throw range.
* All versions don't hit grounded opponents until the fourth active frame, making them 26/28/27 frames startup against them respectively. 
The infamous Leg Tomahawk is an extremely potent neutral tool, especially after making the opponent block a fireball. Its huge range and anti-projectile capabilities mean the opponent always has to be watching out for it. 

In advantage, it's also a good option for ending blockstrings to catch movement, backdashes, and some buttons. They can all be jabbed or High Dodge Attacked on reaction, however, so be careful not to overuse them. 
}}

